e, but I had two \\u2014 wait no: for **Chi B6**, I need to contribute B5 and B7 from hand, plus discarded B6.\\n\\nSo I lose one B5 and one B7.\\n\\nOriginal: B5:1, B6:2, B7:2\\n\\nAfter Chi B6:\\n- Use B5, B7 \\u2192 gone\\n- Discarded B6 taken \\u2192 added to hand temporarily\\n- Form meld [B5,B6,B7]\\n- Remaining: B6:2 (original) - 0 (not used) + 1 (from discard) - 1 (used in meld)? No.\\n\\nClarify: in **Chi**, I use two tiles from hand and the discarded tile to form the meld.\\n\\nSo for [B5,B6,B7]:\\n- I must have B5 and B7 in hand.\\n- Discarded tile is B6.\\n- So I use B5 and B7 from hand, combine with B6 \\u2192 form meld.\\n\\nTherefore, after chi:\\n- B5: 1 \\u2192 0\\n- B7: 2 \\u2192 1\\n- B6: 2 \\u2192 2 (unchanged, not used)\\n- Add meld [B5,B6,B7]\\n\\nSo hand: T1, T2, B6\\u00d72, B7\\u00d71, F1, F3, J2 \\u2192 8 tiles, then discard one \\u2192 7 left before draw.\\n\\nSimilarly, for **Peng B6**:\\n- I have B6\\u00d72, discarded B6 \\u2192 use all three to form pung.\\n- So B6: 2 \\u2192 0\\n- Add meld [B6,B6,B6]\\n- Hand: T1, T2, B5, B7\\u00d72, F1, F3, J2 \\u2192 8 tiles, discard one.\\n\\nSo after either action, same number.\\n\\nNow, which is better?\\n\\nAfter **Peng B6**, I keep B5 and B7\\u00d72 \\u2014 could aim for [B5,B6,B7] later, but B6 is now mostly gone (only one left in wall), hard.\\n\\nOr aim for [B7,B7] pair and wait.\\n\\nBut B7 has 3 unshown, one used in across player\\u2019s meld? Across has [B3,B4,B5], not B7. B7 unshown: 3 \\u2014 so plenty.\\n\\nBut more importantly: **Dragon Pung**? I have J2 \\u2014 one Red Dragon? J2 is Green Dragon.\\n\\nJ2: Green Dragon.\\n\\nI have only one J2 \\u2014 no pung.\\n\\nF1 and F3: North and East Wind? Seat wind is North (F4), prevalent is South (F2). So F1 (East), F3 (West) \\u2014 neither prevalent nor seat wind. So **Prevalent Wind** and **Seat Wind** patterns not triggerable.\\n\\nNo honor pungs.\\n\\nBack to choice.\\n\\nIf I **Peng B6**, I lock in a pung of B6. But B6 is even number \\u